t(1, 1960, """170 or 195 countries without a visa .. The global political climate may determine the number .. My expectation, and Allah knows best, is that it will reach 195""")

t(2, 790, """A symbolic picture that does not express the real manner, but it is symbolic for the lesson .. symbolic for understanding .. symbolic for comprehension .. symbolic for waking many from the coma of illusion and the wrong ideas their minds have woven, because they understood nothing of the real, original story .. and only listened to the tales of legends .. He cries out among the people: Do you allow him chicken once a week? Do you allow him three eggs for dinner? Is there anyone among you who does not eat? Is there anyone among you who sleeps hungry? Is there anyone among you who does not have his daily food? If there is such a one among you, let him cry out now at the top of his voice, and let him show himself now.""")

t(2, 2310, """Symbolic pictures of a symbolic appearance and form, and the picture expresses a truth beyond dispute; it is a terrifying truth for everyone who did not understand this from the beginning .. and a painful truth for everyone who understood early, and the pictures remind him of the pain, while what his state says to the Ummah on that day is: Do you allow me to take a tent from your wealth?""")

t(3, 1185, """I was asked why I linked the Third World War with the fulfilment of the condition in the saying of the Prophet ﷺ about the earth: (as it was filled with injustice and oppression)
The answer: Because war is the greatest degree of injustice a human being is subjected to by those who take the decision of war (as long as it is not a war in defence of religion, honor and land), on his behalf, as a human who needs security, shelter, livelihood, peace of mind, seeking provision and obtaining his needs. So when some person in the world, or a group of influential persons who run the world, takes the decision to bring mankind into a great destructive war, then injustice and oppression have covered the whole earth, because all people will, on account of that war, enter a stage of loss of security, a stage of the shedding of their blood, a stage of their displacement and flight, a stage of the loss of their wealth, a stage of their hunger and thirst, and every evil and every fear will spread on the earth .. After all this injustice, can it be said: injustice and oppression did not cover the earth when this war occurs?

Accordingly, the summary: the world war will mean that injustice and oppression have become realised in all people, not in 70% or 85% of them, because the Prophet ﷺ said: it was filled; and "filled" does not hold while 10% or 15% of people are in ease, comfort, security, safety and peace of mind and the injustice falling on them = zero; then the hadith would not have been fulfilled.""")

t(3, 2045, """Have the people of Palestine been housed? Have the people of Egypt been housed? Have the people of Syria been housed? Have the people of Iraq been housed? Have the people of Iran been housed? Have the people of Pakistan been housed? Have the people of Yemen been housed? Have the people of Morocco been housed? Have the people of Algeria been housed? Have the people of the Arabian Peninsula been housed? Have the people of Tunisia been housed? Have the people of Sudan been housed? Have the people of Somalia been housed? Have the people of Djibouti been housed? Have the people of the Comoros been housed? Have the people of Nigeria been housed? Have the people of Chad been housed? Have the people of Mauritania been housed? Have the people of …. This is the truth .. and whoever does not know this does not know the truth! And many people think it a light matter!""")

t(4, 1125, """Reaching the hard crust saves you 50% of the cost of building your house .. your house is then built using only 5% rebar""")

t(4, 2380, """To those who asked me about the possible river of Jerusalem, Allah the Exalted willing""")

t(5, 1155, """Licences for social and religious lectures .. the end of the age of lecture chaos .. Everyone who flounders in his thinking advises and guides people, while it is not known whether he is guided, astray, or a gatherer of firewood by night!""")

t(5, 2420, """No wife who marries a paralysed man may inform society of that. This is an assault on the husband's dignity. There is no justification and not a single reason that permits a wife to tell society of her husband's disability. This is a moral crime that cannot possibly have any acceptable justification in the religion. Every woman who has married a man with a problem is forbidden to announce it to society, to spread his problem and to wrong him in this way. The problem is that one who committed this grave violation of the Shari'ah should take the lead in family reform.""")

t(6, 1265, """Your parents' maid is not a maid for your wife. Your parents' maid enters the country to serve your parents; otherwise the matter becomes a trick, and you become unjust to your parents and undutiful to them.""")

t(6, 2535, """In the era of the Muslims of the future, Allah the Exalted willing .. a man will be able to bring a maid for his parents, who live in the apartment next to his apartment""")

t(7, 1385, """In the era of the Muslims of the future, Allah the Exalted willing .. a bell in the home of your wife and children .. in case of emergencies""")

t(8, 160, """In the era of the Muslims of the future, Allah the Exalted willing .. Someone asks: How do I serve my parents when I am married? Let your apartment be opposite your parents' apartment and the matter becomes easy for you. If your mother and your wife are on good terms, perhaps she will draw near to Allah through your mother and father; and if they are not on good terms, you have more right to serve your father and mother. And if you are working, that is an era in which workers and servants will come to the lands of the Muslims! And if the relationship between your wife and your mother is bad, the grandchildren go to their grandparents and take the food to them .. Allah is the One whose help is sought; the homes of Muslims are in ruins, between the injustice of husbands' mothers and fathers and the injustice of wives towards husbands' fathers and mothers, as if devils had settled in the homes; but beautiful patience, Allah willing. The picture: two adjacent apartments.""")

t(8, 1755, """The Auja river is a main river in Palestine that flows all year round and springs from 2000 water sources .. The picture is an imagined view of the river as it divides the city of Gaza into two halves to pour into the Mediterranean Sea""")

t(9, 160, """First, the name Yathrib was tied to Medina before the Hijrah, then it was tied to the censure of the hypocrites who lived there with the Prophet ﷺ. Accordingly we learned when young that using the name "Yathrib" is disliked: a prohibition of dislike, not of forbiddance. So why did the Prophet ﷺ use the word "Yathrib" in his hadith about the end of time? This is a matter that caught my attention this moment and had not caught it before. What is understood is that Medina on that day is a mixture of the righteous and the wicked, so it is not known whether the righteous there outweigh the wicked or the reverse; therefore the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah knows best, said "Yathrib" and did not say "Tabah" or "Taybah" or "Medina".

Second, the hadith is clearly specific about the order of events .. The population of Medina the Illuminated decreases only because of the conquest of Jerusalem and people moving to it out of love of living there, it being a great capital at that time, and not the Jerusalem of simple buildings that we see today. So Medina falls into ruin while in its best and most beautiful state, with only a few people remaining in it. This does not at all require that it be absolutely empty; rather, when a city accustomed to being visited by millions of people every year, whose roads are crowded all year long, has that bustle fall to, say, a quarter, this is ruin and is counted as ruin. So when the state of Medina becomes like this, await the Great Battle and its time.""")

t(9, 1020, """The problems of women in their lives have become so entangled that they make a person lose his mind .. It is better for them to understand first what they themselves want, before the whole of society understands what they want, because perhaps they will not understand all that they want, whatever they do!""")

t(9, 2290, """It takes hold of the mentality of many .. many, not all .. many of (the Arabs), because generalising is an intellectual lapse that means nothing but shallow thought and a superficial mind. Many Arabs are taken hold of by sanctifying people and exaggerating in praising them using unsuitable means. Praise is not a crime; we all praise the doer of good, the speaker of what is right, and whoever achieves something of benefit for others and for himself. But we praise with what is permitted in our religion, (May Allah reward you with good .. May Allah bless you .. and any permitted saying) .. Praise is a spontaneous human reaction that we do not plan. As for exaggerating in praise by wasting money that people donate to achieve accomplishments on the ground, this praise did not happen to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, as he entered Jerusalem humbly on his donkey .. nor was it given to the Drawn Sword of Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, as he entered the cities of Iraq or the towns of al-Sham as a victorious conqueror .. And if Jerusalem, by the permission of Allah the Exalted, were liberated tomorrow, and it will be liberated by the permission of Allah the Exalted, and roses were thrown upon its conqueror, then public money would have been wasted and theft of public money would have occurred.""")

t(10, 1430, """Wasting and squandering donors' money in associations lies between theft, when the money is public, and a mentality of wasting and squandering money, when it is from one's own pocket .. A famous woman lecturer enters the headquarters of a women's association to give a lecture and does not object to the wrong! What kind of lectures and thought will she offer people?!""")

t(11, 140, """Issuing a financial support card for a newborn child >> People no longer fear the costs of spending on children""")

t(11, 1390, """The second universal era of Islam: how do we understand its very many details? Read to learn the reason for these pictures in the post.
From Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "At the end of my Ummah the Mahdi will come forth; Allah will give him the life-giving rain, the earth will bring forth its vegetation, he will give out wealth evenly, livestock will multiply and the Ummah will become great; he will live seven or eight", meaning years.
Explanation of part of the hadith:
"The end of my Ummah" means shortly before the Day of Resurrection. "Ghayth", not "matar": for matar (rain) is tied to punishment, while ghayth in Qur'anic wording is tied to mercy, growth and good. "The earth will bring forth its vegetation" means no desert; otherwise the normal state of things is that people water the garden, the crop grows, and the garden's soil brings forth its crop even if the state and its people are disbelievers. So what would be the point of distinguishing the time of the Mahdi by the earth bringing forth its vegetation if the matter referred to gardens and fields! We pause at the earth bringing forth its vegetation, which is what is specifically meant by this post. The inhabitants of our region have been used to living in vast deserts, and the West and the East have boasted over us of the mild air of their land, the breezes of their beautiful countries, and the pleasantness of life amid crops, water and air. The Arabs were the least of nations in crops, the least of nations in water, and the least of nations in mild air. So the hadith is glad tidings for the lands of the Arabs, by the power of Allah our Mighty Lord, that they are about to be clothed, by Allah's permission, in the colour green, and that the colour yellow will disappear from them, by the power of Allah our Mighty Lord, sanctified be His names, magnified in the heavens and on earth, and exalted greatly on high.""")

t(12, 880, """After reading the hadith, look at the pictures to understand. In the Musnad of Imam Ahmad: from Rashid ibn Sa'd, who said: When Istakhr was conquered, a caller cried out: "Lo, the Dajjal has come forth!" He said: Al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah met them and said: "Were it not for what you are saying, I would tell you that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The Dajjal will not come forth until people are heedless of mentioning him, and until the imams stop mentioning him on the pulpits." """)

t(14, 160, """Today even the woman of corrupt conduct, who is abused in the marital home with a violence far from the spirit of the Shari'ah, says: I keep silent about the abuse because I have nowhere to go .. and my family are not a family, a family in name only .. This woman, in the second universal era of Islam, has no excuse to stay in the house of an unjust, harmful man, because the second universal era of Islam solves all the financial problems of people, men and women, and not of men only.""")

t(14, 605, """When the second universal era of Islam is established .. and when 100% of men become owners of wealth, there will remain no excuse for a single man to beat his wife in a way that violates the Shari'ah .. No man on that day can say: I am poor and cannot divorce her .. or: I am poor and forced to keep her as a wife despite her faults and her calamities of conduct because I cannot marry another .. All these claims will fall .. Wealth is empowerment .. and whoever is empowered and brings excuses, all his excuses are thrown back at him .. On that day the punishments will be real and painful for everyone who brings an excuse that does not stand .. and for everyone who thinks Indian films are possible!""")

t(14, 1115, """Hotels that excel at holding wedding parties: the amount of extravagance and wasted money in them is complete ingratitude for blessing .. real ingratitude for blessing .. something that brings the wrath of the Mighty Lord .. an excess that strips the blessing from the life of the bride and groom before their life begins .. feeding the rich and forgetting the hungry poor""")

t(14, 2415, """I remembered the catastrophe of our Egyptian brothers when they marry, which is like the catastrophe of the Pakistanis and the Indian Muslims too when they marry, and I remembered a scene that cannot be separated from the scenes of establishing justice in Muslim society.
The law bans "the list"; a list-of-movables document cannot be notarised; this is contrary to Islam. This procedure is prohibited and punished by law, and the law punishes the bride's sharing in any costs of the marriage or of furnishing a home.""")

t(15, 1345, """Those who emigrate to Palestine in the future are two kinds of people: either those whom longing for what they left behind will not tire much, or those who will tire and turn back to their towns, worn down by yearning for their old life! As for this longing and weariness for the homeland, Allah the Exalted has spared this matter to whomever He has spared among His servants, so that the whole earth has become for him only a station, not a love, nor a passion, nor a soul in pain, pulled by yearning, exhausted by the obstacles to return and wearied by attachments; for all of this is among the marks of man's weakness, not his strength, and it is one of the causes that scatter the human mind. This is the cause the Companions treated with the Prophet ﷺ over 11 years in Medina. So when Mecca, may Allah the Exalted honor it, was conquered and the Prophet ﷺ returned to Medina, the Companions had come a long way in ridding themselves of attachment to the homeland, despite the great rank of Mecca the Honored, no doubt. So they stayed in Medina after him ﷺ, many of them, until al-Sham was conquered and many of them emigrated to it. They were no longer attached either to Medina or to Mecca, may Allah the Exalted honor them both. Their experience of the first emigration to Medina, in the time of weakness, was the forging and the training for them to set out into the world without this psychological weight that people carry when they say: We want to live in our homeland .. So the forging of the people of the first universal era of Islam was a harsh forging that made them as hard as iron. This hardness is important for everyone in the future of the Ummah, and this hardness is realised today in a number of Muslims from various lands who are not worn down by longing for those lands of theirs.""")

t(16, 1985, """The hadith: "A group of my Ummah will remain upholding the command of Allah; those who forsake them will not harm them, nor those who oppose them, ""until the command of Allah comes"", while they prevail over the people" .. and in one narration, "until the Hour comes to them"
Explanation: The command of Allah is the empowerment of the Ummah and its victory through the establishment of its second universal era; it is not the sign of the Smoke, if by that is meant the destruction of the Muslims. For the command of Allah the Exalted is not a punishment that descends upon the Muslims.
As for the narration ""until the Hour comes to them"", it means the portents of the Hour and its great events.

As for the hadith: from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «A band of my Ummah will remain steadfast upon the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; those who oppose it will not harm it; it fights its enemies. Whenever one war ends, the war of another people breaks out; Allah turns the hearts of a people astray to provide for them from them, until the Hour comes to them like pieces of the dark night, and they are terrified by that until they put on coats of armor for it». And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «They are the people of al-Sham», and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the ground with his finger, pointing with it towards al-Sham, until he hurt it).
Some said the pieces of the dark night are the sign of the Smoke! So the sign of the Smoke terrifies them! Then what has the sign of the Smoke to do with armor? The sign of the Smoke is not a war for them to put on armor for it. The hadith speaks of a war .. putting on armor means war .. so putting on armor has nothing to do with the sign of the Smoke .. Therefore the pieces of the dark night are not the darkness of the sign of the Smoke but a metaphor for the severity of the matter .. the severity of the war .. The wars and trials of the Duhayma have been described as pieces of the dark night; we have evidences for the description of the wars and trials of the Duhayma as pieces of the dark night. So the pieces of the dark night here are the Great Battle, which is the invasion of the Romans with 960 thousand soldiers heading for the lands of al-Sham. The Muslims are struck with terror, because it is the Great Battle after which no spoils will be rejoiced in, and after which no inheritance will be divided, and the sons of one father, who were a hundred, will count one another and only one of them remains; so naturally …""")

t(17, 400, """Our Ummah will not be destroyed by the sign of the Smoke, nor by an event containing a punishment that covers it and destroys it. For destruction by a heavenly punishment has been lifted from it as an honor to the Prophet ﷺ. So there is no destruction for our Ummah like Noah's people, 'Ad, Thamud and others.

From Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day from al-'Aliyah, and when he passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah he entered and prayed two rak'ahs in it, and we prayed with him. He supplicated his Lord at length, then turned to us and said ﷺ: "I asked my Lord for three things; He gave me two and withheld one. I asked my Lord not to destroy my Ummah by famine, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to destroy my Ummah by drowning, and He granted me that. And I asked Him not to set their violence among themselves, and He withheld that from me."
Narrator: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas | Hadith scholar: Muslim | Source: Sahih Muslim""")

t(17, 1045, """A Muslim woman holding Dutch citizenship was refused the grant of a plot of land!""")

t(17, 2260, """A brief word to our brothers in the West, may Allah be their help .. Our brothers there will in the future be two groups, with no third .. One group will be gladdened by the future of its Ummah, which is of course in the unseen of Allah the Exalted, its time known to none but Allah the Exalted, and will return for good to build its Ummah out of love and loyalty to it; and one group will return wishing to hold two citizenships, a Western one and that of its Ummah. But I would like to tell the second group that the Prophet ﷺ said:
"You will make a secure truce with the Romans" .. and it will be a real truce, not a cold peace treaty .. Indeed it is clear from the wording of the hadith that it is cooperation, and from the word "secure" several clear and evident meanings are taken. "Secure" is from security, and so security cooperation is clear in the context of the Prophet's ﷺ words. Hence the question that will always be raised: will the West give up the data of those residing in it? The answer is yes, it will hand it over. And will the West give up the data of the Muslims naturalised in it? The answer is yes, it will hand it over .. These are matters of the future .. We are not speaking of the reality of our Ummah today nor of the reality of the world today .. For the secure truce is crowned after 9 years, if the number 9 comes true, from the hadith of the seven or eight""")

t(18, 155, """or nine; this secure truce of nine years is a truce crowned with a war of alliance, and wars of alliance are the highest degree of cooperation of all, and mean that relations are close, firm and strong. In the picture, a Muslim woman holding Belgian citizenship is refused employment in a government office.""")

t(18, 1565, """A Muslim woman who refused to give up her Western citizenship is barred from receiving a grant from the Bayt al-Mal""")

t(19, 345, """A Muslim woman recorded in the government's data as holding a Western citizenship is refused the grant of a government house""")

t(19, 1580, """No nation becomes great without knowing that everyone who holds an additional citizenship is a project of betrayal of his nation, sooner or later .. That is how the Chinese, for example, see it; and such is our Ummah in 2025, 100 years after it was shattered: it no longer possesses a global intelligence power and has fallen back to zero in its intelligence power. So, this being its state, it is better for it to see what the Chinese see and to apply what they apply! A woman holding German citizenship was refused the grant of the new citizenship! It is recorded in her data that she holds German citizenship! This is the fruit of: "You will make a secure truce with the Romans" .. The sharing of the data of Muslim subjects residing in the West is one of the many fruits of the secure truce! The post and the picture are an important analysis for understanding the hadith: "and the Ummah will become great" .. and the hadith: "You will make a secure truce with the Romans".""")
